      "path": "services/workers/tests/test_parsing_gapfill.py",
      "reason": "test_class_expression_nested_in_a_function_chains_its_qualified_names (@spec EC-12) originally asserted _function_names(result) == [\"m\"], i.e. that the enclosing function f(){...} would be absent from result.functions. That contradicts EC-12's own spec.md text (which only specifies C.qualified_name, m.qualified_name, m.enclosing_class) and pre-existing declared-OK GAP-2 behavior (a named top-level function_declaration is always extracted). Changed the assertion to check \"m\" in _function_names(result) and select the method by its exact qualified_name instead of assuming list length/order."
    }
